    "content": "The Deputy President of Puntland, Ilyas Osman Lugatoor, participated in a ceremony in Garowe on Monday to mark World Humanitarian Day. The event brought together government officials, aid workers, and community representatives to honor the contributions of humanitarian personnel in the region.\n\nWorld Humanitarian Day is observed annually on August 19, designated by the United Nations to raise awareness about humanitarian assistance and to pay tribute to those who have lost their lives in humanitarian service. This year's commemoration in Puntland focused on the ongoing challenges faced by vulnerable populations, including internally displaced persons and those affected by drought and conflict.\n\nIn his remarks, Lugatoor acknowledged the critical role humanitarian organizations play in providing lifesaving support across Puntland. He reiterated the government's commitment to facilitating safe and unhindered access for aid workers, while also calling for greater international solidarity to address the region's humanitarian needs.\n\nPuntland, a semi-autonomous state in northeastern Somalia, has faced recurrent humanitarian crises exacerbated by climatic shocks and insecurity. The observance of this day serves as a reminder of the resilience of communities and the importance of sustained humanitarian investment.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this event underscores the ongoing need for support to humanitarian efforts in their homeland. Diaspora remittances and advocacy remain vital lifelines for many families, and the day's recognition highlights the collective responsibility to uphold humanitarian values.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/puntland-oo-laga-xusay-maalinta-biniaadantinimada-adduunka/424985/",
